<%#
Cistergraphia: the plate (fol. 2r)
==================================

Purpose:
- Show the generated Cistergraphia and let the user keep it

Design Decisions:
- The SVG is shown on the leaf in ink colours (CSS only); exports stay the
  plain black-on-white file that the decoder reads
- Strokes are inked in reading order and dry from rubric to ink (JS), so the
  snail is visible; the plate can be walked sign by sign (pointer or arrow keys)
- The scribe's job is to send: Download SVG leads, right under the specs. The
  lede says what Read will open for the reader; the bench and the board below
  are a preview of that puzzle
- "Read it back" posts the same SVG to /decode with decipher=1: the decoder's
  answer, since the scribe knows it (a reader's damaged plate opens as its puzzle)
- Rongorongo plates can be turned half round (JS, CSS only): the turned rows
  then read upright, as the readers of Rapa Nui turned their tablets
- A grille's plate shows its key, and its grille: the stencil (the server's,
  embedded once) is laid over the plate and turned N, E, S, W, lighting the
  signs under its holes; the same file downloads, to print and cut. The key
  goes along with "Read it back"
- A weathered plate shows its lacunae; walking a worn sign says it is worn,
  never its value (the page must not hold the answer)
- The restoration bench (weathered plates): choose a lacuna on the plate (a
  sign with one lacuna is chosen by its whole cell) or step through them,
  press a digit back in, and the pair is weighed; a count says how many are
  restored. The page
  only knows what the file shows, so it says whether pairs balance, never
  whether a restoration is right: the words, and Read it back, decide. Its
  first state is drawn by the server, so nothing moves when the script arrives
- A broken plate shows its board and, below it, the tray of fragments. With
  the script, the fragments move: drag one, or pick it and then a cell of
  the board for its top-left corner; arrow keys move a picked fragment by a
  cell, T or a double click turns it half round. Once they cover the board,
  the page weighs every pair along both reading paths, and says how many
  balance. The page holds what the file shows, never where a fragment goes.
  A weathered broken plate is weighed by what each worn sign may hold; whole
  again, it reads as an edition (there is no bench on a plate in pieces)
- Nothing moves while you walk or turn the plate: the live reading takes the
  resting caption's place, and the script-only controls have their space from
  the first paint

Constraints:
- Copy/download need JS; the inline SVG can always be saved from the page
%>
<section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="plate-title">
  <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 2<sup>r</sup></p>
  <h1 id="plate-title" class="rubric"><%= @secret ? 'Your sealed Cistergraphia' : 'Your Cistergraphia' %></h1>

  <p class="message-echo"><span class="visually-hidden">Message: </span><q><%= @message %></q></p>
  <% if @decoy %>
    <p class="decoy-echo"><span class="label">For the novice</span> <q><%= @decoy %></q></p>
  <% end %>
  <% if @pieces && @damage %>
    <p class="lede">Ruined: <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>, <%= lacunae_count(@damage.size) %>. Download it and send it: Read opens it for your reader as the board, to rejoin by what each worn sign may hold, then as the edition to restore. Below, a preview of their puzzle.</p>
  <% elsif @pieces %>
    <p class="lede">Broken: <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>. Download it and send it: Read opens it for your reader as the board, where only the sums say where each fragment goes. Below, a preview of their puzzle.</p>
  <% elsif @damage %>
    <p class="lede">Worn: <%= lacunae_count(@damage.size) %>. Download it and send it: Read opens it for your reader as the bench, where each pair must balance again and the words settle the doubts. Below, a preview of their puzzle.</p>
  <% elsif @secret %>
    <p class="lede">Secret mode: sealed with your passphrase. Without it, this plate reveals nothing but its length.</p>
  <% elsif @normalized != @message %>
    <p class="lede">Enciphered as: <code><%= @normalized %></code></p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="lede">A game: anyone patient enough can read it back.</p>
  <% end %>

  <dl class="specs">
    <div><dt>Mode</dt><dd><%= @secret ? 'Secret' : 'Game' %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Signs</dt><dd><%= @symbols %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd><%= Integer.sqrt(@symbols) %> × <%= Integer.sqrt(@symbols) %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Layout</dt><dd><%= layout_name(@layout) %></dd></div>
    <% if @pieces && @damage %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Ruined: <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %>, worn</dd></div>
    <% elsif @pieces %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Broken, in <%= fragments_count(@pieces.size) %></dd></div>
    <% elsif @damage %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Worn</dd></div>
    <% end %>
    <% if grille? && @decoy %>
      <div><dt>Abbot’s key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Novice’s key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout.novice %></code></dd></div>
    <% elsif grille? %>
      <div><dt>Grille key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" data-action="download-svg">Download SVG</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="download-png">Download PNG</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-action="copy-svg">Copy SVG code</button>
    <% if @layout == :rongorongo %>
      <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="turn-plate" aria-pressed="false">Turn the plate</button>
    <% end %>
    <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/">Inscribe another</a>
  </div>

  <% if @pieces %>
    <%== erb :_board, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, fragments: @fragments, size: Integer.sqrt(@symbols), worn: !@damage.nil? } %>
  <% else %>
    <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, cells: plate_cells_json(@sequence, @layout, @damage || {}), geometry: plate_layout_json(@sequence, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: @decoy } %>
  <% end %>

  <% if @damage && !@pieces %>
    <%== erb :_bench, layout: false, locals: { entries: lacunae(@sequence, @layout, @damage), values: @sequence, damage: @damage, tally: nil } %>
  <% end %>

  <% if grille? %>
    <% grilles = plate_grilles %>
    <div class="actions grille-actions">
      <% if grilles.size > 1 %>
        <div class="segments grille-choice awaits-script" role="group" aria-label="Which grille to lay">
          <% grilles.each_with_index do |grille, i| %>
            <button type="button" class="segment" data-grille-choice="<%= grille[:part] %>" aria-pressed="<%= i.zero? %>"><span class="segment-title"><%= grille[:part] == :abbot ? 'Abbot' : 'Novice' %></span></button>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary awaits-script" data-action="lay-grille" aria-pressed="false">Lay the grille</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="download-stencil"><%= grilles.size > 1 ? 'Download the stencils' : 'Download the stencil' %></button>
      <% grilles.each do |grille| %>
        <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="copy-key" data-key="<%= grille[:key] %>"><%= grilles.size > 1 ? "Copy #{grille[:label].sub('grille', 'key')}" : 'Copy the key' %></button>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <% grilles.each do |grille| %>
      <template data-stencil="<%= grille[:part] %>" data-label="<%= grille[:label] %>" data-path="<%= grille[:path] %>"><%== grille[:stencil] %></template>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>


  <form class="readback" method="post" action="/decode">
    <h2 class="index-heading">Read it back</h2>
    <input type="hidden" name="svg" value="<%= @svg_content %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="decipher" value="1">
    <% if grille? %><input type="hidden" name="grille" value="<%= @layout %>"><% end %>
    <div class="readback-row">
      <% if @secret %>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="readback-passphrase">Passphrase</label>
          <div class="passphrase">
            <input type="password" id="readback-passphrase" name="passphrase" autocomplete="current-password"
                   autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" required>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Decode this plate</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
